      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "REAL CHANCE (7) hit the ground running with a slick early sectional but had to settle for a minor placing when a 2.25 lengths third over 318m at this track, clocking 18.48. Key chance in this line up. ADA TARO (3) is a quick beginner who took advantage of the inside draw, flying the boxes and leading throughout to score (18.55) at this track in Grade 4/5 over 318m. Brilliant beginner who should be leading the way here. Has hit winning form and can go on with it. HARD STYLE CHICK (2) missed the frame and was safely held latest finishing 7th at this track following on from a third place finish (18.60) there the start prior. Has a good record here at this journey. The form out of the last run is proven to be strong. Has the ability to give this a shake. SHIFTY BULLDOZER (8) comes off a (22.66) win last time, scoring by 5 lengths in a Grade 3/4 over 400m at Wagga. Loves this draw, having won three of five starts.",
